Description: Analyzes Cayley graphs of permutation puzzles. Any puzzle
    whose moves permute a fixed set of positions can be declared as a
    permutation group, and the same tools then work on it: cycle
    detection, state space exploration and path search. Two puzzles are
    built in: TopSpin and Rubik's cubes of any size. The 3x3x3 is solved
    by four human methods and by a two-phase search after Herbert
    Kociemba; the 4x4x4 is solved by reduction.
    The Iterative Cycle Intersection (ICI) method is described in Yuri
    Baramykov (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2607.13219>.
